    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "NOTEL TAMANACO\nCORREOS\nFESTIVAL DEL\nAMERICA\nCARACAS\nLIBRO\nXVENEZUELA\nHOTEL TAMANACO CARACAS\nHOTEL TAMANACO• CARACAS\nUN HOTEL INTERCONTINENTAL\nCORREOS\nREPUBLICA DE VENEZUE\nFLORREO-\nREPUBLICA DE VENEZUELA\nCARACAS - VENEZUELA\nACAS 0\nPRIMER DIA DE EMISION\nFIRST DAY OF ISSUE\nMr. Harold M. Bixby, Director\nPan American\n1 World Airways\n135 East 42nd Street\nNew York 17, New York\nPOR AVION\nAIRMA TL",
      "HOTEL\nTAMANACO\nUN HOTEL INTERCONTINENTAL\nCaracas. October 10. 1957\nDear Sir:\nTo-day is the first day of issue of the Hotel\nTamanaco postage stamp, and we are availing our-\nselves of this opportunity to convey our greetings\nto you.\nOn the eve of the 4th anniversary of the Tamanaco,\nwe are proud to have its facsimile travel around\nthe world as a symbol of the traditional hospit-\nality and friendship of Venezuela.\nWe hope that this stamped envelope of philatelic\ninterest may form\npart of your collectión, or\nbring back pleasant memories of your visit with us.\nCordially yours,\nSam\nR. L. Lambert\nGeneral Manager\nTELFS: 33.711 - 33.741 - CABLE: INHOTELCOR\nA PARTADO 467 - CARA CAS\n- VENEZUELA"
    ],
